  {
   "unit": "L1/H2",
   "slug": "EleutherAI--pythia-70m/L1/H2",
   "kind": "head",
   "share": 0.002262964862357743,
   "attribution": 0.5746448040008545,
   "status": "VERIFIED",
   "explanation": "Dense previous-token head that crosses the line on almost any text longer than a few tokens: strongest on the second piece of a word or name the tokenizer splits (Mac|mill, Mc|Av, bark|ed, cheer|ed), the token after ' there' ('s, is, be), an abbreviation's period, whitespace runs, list numbers, URLs and code, and it also crosses on the 2nd-4th tokens of any text that does not open with 'The' (A dog ate..., He kicked..., Mary won...) and on the token after ' and', ' on', ' over', ' near', ' all' or ' first'. It stays below the line only on (a) one single-token word followed by '.' ('Water.', 'Sorry.', 'True.') and (b) texts made only of 'The'-opened simple clauses of single-token everyday words, 'The N.', 'The N V.' or 'The N V the N.', one or several in a row, with no split word, adjective, preposition, 'and', comma, number, pronoun or name (known exceptions that still fire: ' door', ' way', ' other', ' same', ' time' after 'the').",
